  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Restoring the Tailwind Flip**\n\nOkay, so I just realized I accidentally deleted the `.is-flipped` CSS in the Tailwind refactor. It\'s supposed to handle the card flip, so I\'m putting that back in. Specifically, the line is `.is-flipped .card-inner { transform: rotateY(180deg); }`. I\'m also relocating the filter buttons to the header in `index.html`, and updating their style.\n\n\n**Refining the Tab Buttons**\n\nI\'m tackling the tab button styling. Currently, the active state is handled inconsistently between HTML and JavaScript. The `index.html` has pre-defined Tailwind styles for both active and inactive states. JS only adds/removes `.active`, which does not switch the Tailwind styles. My current approach involves simplifying the HTML by removing hardcoded styles and allowing CSS to handle the `.active` state change. I am refactoring the tab button styles in `index.html` and `index.css` to fix it.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 72670758
    }
