  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Button Malfunction**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the button uses `.btn-flip`. Now I\'m shifting focus to why the \"\343\201\223\343\201\237\343\201\210\343\202\222\343\201\277\343\202\213\" button isn\'t working. My hypothesis centers on `z-index` conflicts, potentially hiding the button or the `card-outer` click listener intercepting clicks. The `flipBtn` handles this so there is something amiss.\n\n\n**Analyzing Click Propagation**\n\nI believe I\'ve pinpointed the issue. By using `e.stopPropagation()` and manually toggling `cardWrapper.classList.toggle(\'is-flipped\')`, I should have resolved the direct click blocking. I\'m now examining the impact of `pointer-events`. The `card-outer` wrapper\'s absolute positioning of `card-face` elements might be the culprit. I believe `backface-hidden` applied to both front and back during the Tailwind refactor is significant. When the card flips, the front face becomes invisible, and the back face becomes visible.\n\n\n**Debugging Event Bubbling**\n\nI\'m now back-tracking and reassessing the event handling. The issue doesn\'t appear to be related to the propagation direction from the container. My analysis shows that `e.stopPropagation()` on the button only prevents it from bubbling up the DOM, not from affecting the button itself. The issue isn\'t even event bubbling, and instead, it may be the CSS. I\'m checking if `.is-flipped` CSS was missing, and the answer is yes.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 339283335
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
